# Generated artifacts. Model weights and per-run JSON are regenerated; the markdown deliverables
# (RESULTS.md, IDEA_EVAL.md, PREREGISTRATION.md) are the write-up and MUST be tracked -- in
# particular PREREGISTRATION.md is only worth anything if its commit timestamp precedes the runs
# it predicts.
# (`artifacts/*` rather than `artifacts/`: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# negation for a file inside one never fires. Excluding the contents instead keeps the negation
# reachable.)
artifacts/*
!artifacts/*.md

# The dataset directory. `data/` holds ONLY data now: the source package that used to live here
# is `devign_data/`. That separation is the point -- an ignore rule written for the dataset once
# swallowed the entire source package of the same name, and this layout makes that impossible.
data/
_smoke/
*.log

# Source bundles built for transferring the code to a training box (see README).
# Regenerated on demand; committing them puts a zip of the repo inside the repo.
*.zip
*.bundle

# Dataset files. The CodeXGLUE release parquets are ~22 MB and are data, not source -- point
# data.real_data_path at wherever they live instead of committing them.
*.parquet

# The Devign paper itself (NeurIPS 2019). Not redistributed here -- read it at
# https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.03496
*.PDF
*.pdf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
